  "body": "[Event relationships](#2674) are currently sent unencrypted so that they may be aggregated server-side.  However, they may contain information that we do not want to be plain-text (e.g. we don't want the server to know if a user reacted with a :+1: or :-1: ).  We should figure out a way to encrypt them.  matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals#1849 includes some [thoughts on how to do encryption](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/blob/matthew/msc1849/proposals/1849-aggregations.md#thoughts-on-encrypting-the-aggregation-key), and sorunome and deepbluev7 have also given some thoughts at https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/1849#discussion_r446515510",
